# android-bionic-0.8.4 — build OpenTUI 0.8.4 (git d4a2af24ba50636da5f222367f91746a1bf89644)
# packages/native for aarch64-linux-android (Termux/bionic). Apply with
# `patch -p1` at the OpenTUI source root before building; verified by
# tools/transplant/build-libopentui-0.8.4.sh.
#
# Why: OpenCode v2 embeds a glibc libopentui.so that cannot dlopen on bionic,
# and the JS FFI layer stores pointers as numbers (safe-integer checked), so
# Android heap-tagged pointers (TBI, top byte 0xb4) are rejected.
#
# Contents:
#   packages/native/build.zig
#     - -Dbionic-libdir / -Dbionic-include / -Dbionic-api cross-build switches
#       for android-abi library builds (system lib dir, merged bionic headers,
#       __ANDROID_API__/__ANDROID_MIN_SDK_VERSION__).
#     - translate-c steps (miniaudio, yoga, context ABI) get the same headers,
#       macros and lib path; the main module links libc on android.
#     - android-untag.c is compiled into the library.
#   packages/native/src/android-untag.c (new)
#     - constructor that calls mallopt(M_BIONIC_SET_HEAP_TAGGING_LEVEL, NONE)
#       so scudo returns canonical (<= 2^53) heap pointers to JS.
#   packages/native/src/buffer.zig
#     - FFI negative-coordinate guards ported to 0.8.4: clamp u32 scissor
#       sizes (mov w, #0x7fffffff), saturating ends (csel ..., vs), bit31
#       setCell early-returns, INT32_MIN negation guards for text/grayscale.
#   packages/native/src/clipboard/host.zig
#     - bionic has no pthread_tryjoin_np; keep the clipboard worker
#       unjoinable instead of referencing a missing symbol.
